What is WSL?

WSL = Windows Subsystem for Linux

Think of it like:

Windows
   |
   └── WSL
        |
        └── Ubuntu
             |
             ├── Bash
             ├── Linux commands
             ├── Git
             ├── Python
             ├── Ansible
             └── other Linux tools

You don't need to dual-boot Windows/Linux, and you don't need a traditional VM just to get a Linux terminal.

